# Budget

// tags group the categories; the views update as you type.
// amounts are rates: /period keeps it in every answer, and the
// totals stay dimension-checked (income mixes /month and /year).
// budget-vs-actual: every category has a paired *_actual variable,
// and the variance section is plain subtraction

## Income
paycheck = 2400/month @income
paycheck_actual = 2380/month @income
side = 4200/year @income
side_actual = 3900/year @income

## Fixed
rent = 950/month @fixed
rent_actual = 950/month @fixed
utilities = 120/month @fixed
utilities_actual = 138/month @fixed
internet = 45/month @fixed
internet_actual = 45/month @fixed

## Variable
groceries = 320/month @variable
groceries_actual = 355/month @variable
transport = 90/month @variable
transport_actual = 74/month @variable
fun = 150/month @fun
fun_actual = 190/month @fun

## The picture
total @income
total @fixed
total @variable
total @fun

## Budget vs actual
// positive variance = under budget
income_var = (paycheck_actual + side_actual) - (paycheck + side)
fixed_var = (rent_actual + utilities_actual + internet_actual) - (rent + utilities + internet)
variable_var = (groceries_actual + transport_actual) - (groceries + transport)
fun_var = fun_actual - fun
total_var = income_var + fixed_var + variable_var + fun_var
